# Remembers a new person, met in the open session, with their facts and
# samples. When no session is open, the call starts one. The person is
# forgotten with the session (walkie-database ADR-0010). Every call stores a
# new person, so a retry after a lost answer may store them twice.

# Empty stores a person whose name is not known. At most 100 characters.
# Spaces at either end are ignored.
string name
# At most 32 facts, each with a different key.
Fact[] facts
# Face samples, for example from different angles. At most 100.
ModelVector[] faces
# Clothing and body samples. They are searched only in this session,
# because clothes change. At most 100. faces and appearances together must
# hold at least one vector, or the person could never be matched.
ModelVector[] appearances
---
# False when nothing was stored. That happens when a vector names a model
# with no table of its kind, has the wrong number of values, is all zeros,
# or holds NaN or infinity, when a limit above is broken, or when the
# database failed. message then says why, and names the field at fault, for
# example "faces[3]". When the database failed, it starts with "The database
# could not". StartSession's response lists the models the node takes.
bool success
# For example "Remembered Sam as person 12 in session 5, from 21 faces and
# 20 appearances."
string message
# person.id of the new person. 0 when success is false.
int64 person_id
# The session the person joined. 0 when success is false.
int64 session_id
